%% Event processing under at-least-once delivery. Rendered copy: event-processing-sequence.svg
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Producer
    participant A as catalog-api
    participant LQ as SQS listing-events
    participant W as Listing consumer (worker)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant R as Outbox relay (worker)
    participant CQ as SQS change-events
    participant M as Matching consumer (worker)
    participant D as Dead-letter queue

    P->>A: POST /api/v1/ingestion/events (1–500 events)
    A->>A: validate every event (rules shared with the sync path)
    A->>LQ: SendMessageBatch
    A-->>P: 202 Accepted {accepted, eventIds}

    W->>LQ: ReceiveMessage (long poll 20 s, visibility 60 s, at most free permits)
    LQ-->>W: message, receiveCount = n
    W->>DB: BEGIN (READ COMMITTED)
    W->>DB: find event id in processed_events
    alt exact replay of a processed event
        DB-->>W: stored outcome, nothing written
    else same event id, different content
        W->>D: dead-letter EVENT_ID_REUSED
    else new event
        W->>DB: lock listing (FOR UPDATE) or INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
        W->>W: decide: newer version, stale, same-version conflict, tombstone
        W->>DB: write listing, INSERT processed_events, INSERT outbox_events
        W->>DB: COMMIT
    end
    W->>LQ: DeleteMessage

    Note over W,LQ: Transient failure: ChangeMessageVisibility with full-jitter backoff (2 s … 5 min).<br/>After 5 receives: explicit DLQ with failureReason. Queue redrive at 6 receives covers a crashed worker.<br/>Permanent failure (malformed JSON, invalid event, unknown source): DLQ at once.

    loop every 250 ms
        R->>DB: claim due rows FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        R->>CQ: SendMessageBatch (ListingChangedV1)
        R->>DB: mark PUBLISHED in the claiming transaction
    end

    CQ-->>M: ListingChangedV1
    M->>DB: retrieve candidates (GTIN, brand + model, title trigram)
    M->>M: score features, apply explicit rules
    M->>DB: upsert match_candidates, link canonical product
    M->>CQ: DeleteMessage
